  "problems": "FRAME has no standalone size-guide page (all /pages/size-guide variants 404); charts live in the per-product 'Size & Fit' modal and were read from the page's embedded data. Values are published in inches; the CM toggle is computed client-side, so inches were recorded. Denim conversion table's first column is headed 'US' but holds the denim size (23-34); UK/IT/FR aliases kept as published. Conflict: size 34 hip is 43.5 in on denim product pages but 44.5 in in the 'Measurements Bottoms (in.)' table on apparel product pages (all other bottoms values match); 43.5 recorded from the denim page. The apparel chart has unusual steps: M waist 27.5-28.5 overlaps S/M 27-27.75, and bust jumps from 36-37 (M/L) to 40-42 (L); both XXS and XS map to FR 32 and US 0/00. Size-spanning sizes 0/1/2 appear in the denim modal of every jean checked (unclear whether they apply to that style). Product modals also show per-style garment specs (rise, inseam, leg opening) for one size, not recorded. Basis is not stated in visible text for any chart."
